{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj | sed -n '1,230p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.cross-lang-test\n     2\t  \"The substrate claim, empirically (yang.antlr.md 8.10/8.11): both preludes\n     3\t   bottom out in `:application`, and the engine neither knows nor cares which\n     4\t   frontend minted a closure. A TypeScript function value is called from\n     5\t   PHP-lowered code and a PHP closure from TypeScript-lowered code, in one\n     6\t   VM, one run.\n     7\t\n     8\t   The seam is the lowered tree, not a prelude change. Each direction lowers\n     9\t   a program normally, then (1) extracts the foreign function value by\n    10\t   running the donor program with its `run-main` replaced so the program's\n    11\t   value IS the function (`js/make-function` cell, `php/make-function` cell),\n    12\t   and (2) binds that value to a free variable of the receiver, replacing the\n    13\t   receiver's lookup node (`php/resolve-fn` of a name; `js/global-get` of a\n    14\t   name) by that variable. Both function values are cells whose `:code` is\n    15\t   called with a receiver slot and an argument vector, so the callee needs no\n    16\t   knowledge of the caller's prelude.\n    17\t\n    18\t   What is pinned as LIMITS (documented expectations, not failures):\n    19\t   a PHP array reaching TypeScript is an opaque handle that only PHP can use;\n    20\t   PHP null (`:php/null`) is neither JS null nor undefined. The JVM lane runs\n    21\t   the AST walker only.\"\n    22\t  (:require\n    23\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    24\t    [clojure.walk :as walk]\n    25\t    [yang.php.antlr.e2e-harness :as php]\n    26\t    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as php-h]\n    27\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.e2e-test :as ts]\n    28\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\n    29\t    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    30\t    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\t(defn- app?\n    34\t  [node op]\n    35\t  (and (map? node)\n    36\t       (= :application (:type node))\n    37\t       (= {:type :variable, :name op} (:operator node))))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t(defn- find-node\n    41\t  \"The first node of `tree` satisfying `pred`, preorder.\"\n    42\t  [pred tree]\n    43\t  (let [hit (volatile! nil)]\n    44\t    (walk/prewalk (fn [n] (when (and (nil? @hit) (pred n)) (vreset! hit n)) n)\n    45\t                  tree)\n    46\t    @hit))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(defn- var-node\n    50\t  [name]\n    51\t  {:type :variable, :name name})\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn- donor\n    55\t  \"The AST whose value is the function value of the donor program: the\n    56\t   `run-main` application becomes a call of its body, which is replaced by\n    57\t   the first function-making node (`make-fn`) of the program.\"\n    58\t  [ast run-main make-fn body-args]\n    59\t  (let [fn-node (find-node #(app? % make-fn) ast)]\n    60\t    (assert fn-node (str \"no \" make-fn \" node in the donor\"))\n    61\t    (walk/prewalk\n    62\t      (fn [n]\n    63\t        (if (app? n run-main)\n    64\t          {:type :application,\n    65\t           :operator {:type :lambda,\n    66\t                      :params ['%body],\n    67\t                      :body {:type :application,\n    68\t                             :operator (var-node '%body),\n    69\t                             :operands body-args}},\n    70\t           :operands [{:type :lambda,\n    71\t                       :params (if (= make-fn 'js/make-function) ['%0] []),\n    72\t                       :body fn-node}]}\n    73\t          n))\n    74\t      ast)))\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\t(defn- lowered-php\n    78\t  [source]\n    79\t  (let [{:keys [ast diagnostics]} (php/lower-program source)]\n    80\t    (assert (nil? diagnostics) (pr-str diagnostics))\n    81\t    ast))\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t(defn- lowered-ts\n    85\t  [source]\n    86\t  (let [r (ts/lower-source source :bundled)]\n    87\t    (assert (nil? (:diagnostics r)) (pr-str (:diagnostics r)))\n    88\t    (let [{:yin/keys [batch root]} (:program r)]\n    89\t      (nth batch root))))\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\t(defn- bind\n    93\t  \"`receiver` with `v-name` bound to the value of `donor-ast`.\"\n    94\t  [donor-ast v-name receiver]\n    95\t  {:type :application,\n    96\t   :operator {:type :lambda, :params [v-name], :body receiver},\n    97\t   :operands [donor-ast]})\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\t(defn- registry\n   101\t  []\n   102\t  (php-h/host-registry))\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\t(defn- run\n   106\t  [ast]\n   107\t  (vm/value (vm/eval (tu/create-vm {:modules (registry)}) ast)))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t(defn ts-into-php\n   111\t  \"PHP `source` calling `ts_fn(...)`, with `ts_fn` the TS function `ts-src`\n   112\t   (a program of one arrow expression). Returns the printed text.\"\n   113\t  [ts-src source]\n   114\t  (let [fn-ast (donor (lowered-ts ts-src) 'js/run-main 'js/make-function\n   115\t                      [{:type :literal, :value :js/undefined}])\n   116\t        php-ast (walk/postwalk\n   117\t                  (fn [n]\n   118\t                    (if (app? n 'php/resolve-fn)\n   119\t                      (var-node '%tsfn)\n   120\t                      n))\n   121\t                  (lowered-php source))]\n   122\t    (php-h/render (run (bind fn-ast '%tsfn php-ast)))))\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\t(defn php-into-ts\n   126\t  \"TS `source` calling `phpfn(...)`, with `phpfn` the PHP closure `php-src`\n   127\t   (a program holding one closure expression). Returns the rendered value.\"\n   128\t  [php-src source]\n   129\t  (let [fn-ast (donor (lowered-php php-src) 'php/run-main 'php/make-function [])\n   130\t        ts-ast (walk/postwalk\n   131\t                 (fn [n]\n   132\t                   (if (and (app? n 'js/global-get)\n   133\t                            (= \"phpfn\" (get-in n [:operands 0 :value :js/str])))\n   134\t                     (var-node '%phpfn)\n   135\t                     n))\n   136\t                 (lowered-ts source))]\n   137\t    (render/output (run (bind fn-ast '%phpfn ts-ast)))))\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   140\t(deftest ts-closure-called-from-php-test\n   141\t  (testing \"a number crosses as a number: float in, float out\"\n   142\t    (is (= \"4\"\n   143\t           (ts-into-php \"(x, y) => x + y;\" \"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5);\"))))\n   144\t  (testing \"the PHP caller sees the result as an ordinary value\"\n   145\t    (is (= \"yes\"\n   146\t           (ts-into-php \"(x, y) => x + y;\"\n   147\t                        \"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5) == 4 ? 'yes' : 'no';\")))))\n   148\t\n   149\t\n   150\t(deftest php-closure-called-from-ts-test\n   151\t  (testing \"TS stores and calls the same PHP function cell it received\"\n   152\t    (is (= {:js/out [\"true 5\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n   153\t           (php-into-ts \"<?php fn($a, $b) => $a + $b;\"\n   154\t                        \"const stored = phpfn; console.log(stored === phpfn, stored(2, 3));\")))))\n   155\t\n   156\t\n   157\t(deftest limits-test\n   158\t  (testing \"a PHP array returned to TS is an opaque handle, usable in PHP\"\n   159\t    (let [src \"<?php fn($a = 7) => $a === 7 ? [1, 2, 3] : count($a);\"]\n   160\t      ;; the PHP int `count` returns reaches TS as an integer (`3n`), not a\n   161\t      ;; JS number: the two preludes keep their own number kinds\n   162\t      (is (= {:js/out [\"3n\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n   163\t             (php-into-ts src \"const h = phpfn(); console.log(phpfn(h));\")))))\n   164\t  (testing \"PHP null is neither JS null nor undefined\"\n   165\t    (let [src \"<?php fn() => null;\"]\n   166\t      (is (= {:js/out [\"false false\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n   167\t             (php-into-ts src\n   168\t                          \"const n = phpfn(); console.log(n === null, n === undefined);\"))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
