ction 7.3, r6). A foreign format or an `:image` the table does not\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:438:                  {:reason :foreign-format,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:72:;;   :foreign-value       a closure or continuation another task minted;\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:74:;;   :foreign-format      a continuation of another kernel format or image\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:88:                {:reason :foreign-value, :kind (values/kind-of f)}))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:868:   continuation another task minted refuses as `:foreign-value`: lift is\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:889:                (non-portable! :foreign-value {:yin.k/hint (values/kind-of x)})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1370:   scheduler verified (act 2, `:foreign-image`); the receiving task then\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1415:                foreign (first (remove origin-of\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1417:            (if (some? foreign)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1420:                               :reason :foreign-image,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1422:                               :segment foreign})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:354:- **Owned.** The owner tag is derived once per task from its capability secret (`values/owner-tag`, held in VM state as `:owner`; nil for a task without a secret). Application refuses a closure another task minted with `:foreign-value`. Lift is the only crossing: the encoder refuses a foreign closure as `:yin.k/non-portable` of kind `:foreign-value`, and `lower-closure` mints with the receiver's owner. A lower takes its binders from the attached lambda, never the wire: a marker whose `:yin.k/params` (named kernels) or `:yin.k/arity` (positional kernels) is not the attached lambda's refuses `:marker-mismatch`, and a non-symbol binder refuses `:non-symbol-parameter` first.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:465:| `:foreign-value` | A closure or continuation another task minted. Carries `:kind :closure` or `:continuation`. |\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:466:| `:foreign-format` | A continuation of another kernel format or image (the positional kernels' restore check). |\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:705:**Evaluation:** Returns a continuation value carrying the current continuation and lexical environment: a `yin.vm.values/Continuation` host type, minted only by a kernel and owned by the capturing task, over the `:reified-continuation` payload map. Like a closure (Part 3) it is unforgeable, opaque to guest `get`, equal by structure, and refused with `:foreign-value` in another task. A continuation never crosses a lift (`:non-canonicalizable`). A `:parked-continuation` stays plain data: resume goes by id through the engine's `:parked` table.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:32:   its canonical bytes and hash. The 'CLJS receiver refuses a foreign\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1095:   or foreign-round result is loss, reported with the append outcome the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:115:**Purpose:** The owner tag every closure and continuation this task mints carries (D7), derived once from the capability secret by `yin.vm.values/owner-tag` in `yin.vm/empty-state` and never revealing it. A task composed without a secret has owner nil. Application and invocation refuse a closure or continuation whose owner is not this task's (`:foreign-value`); the lift encoder refuses one as `:yin.k/non-portable`, and `lower-closure` mints with the receiver's owner. Cell, stream and cursor references are not owner-tagged: they stay sealed plain data.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head.cljc:604:(defn- foreign?\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head.cljc:664:      (foreign? (:kind status))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/head.cljc:671:                            {:yin.head/foreign-kind (:kind status)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
